# Direct dependencies of the `unit-tests` job in .gitlab-ci.yml (T676, SEC-T675-09). That job
# binds the host Docker socket, so nothing in it may float: this file is the human-edited
# input, `requirements-ci.txt` is the hash-locked output and the only file the job installs
# (`pip install --require-hashes --only-binary=:all: -r ci/requirements-ci.txt`).
#
# To change a dependency: edit this file, then regenerate the lock (see docs/wiki/mcp-pin-bump-checklist.md,
# section "CI Python lock files"):
#   uv pip compile ci/requirements-ci.in --universal --python-version 3.12 --generate-hashes --exclude-newer <UTC timestamp> -o ci/requirements-ci.txt
# <UTC timestamp> is a cooldown (SEC-T676-14): at least 7 days before the generation day, never the day itself, and
# every new or changed package must be at least 14 days old (check its PyPI upload time).
# tests/functional/test_ci_hash_pins.py fails when an input has no locked version or the two files drift.
